VALUES ('159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 'dca-orchestration-swarm-stacks-deep-dive', 'DCA Practice: Orchestration Deep Dive — Swarm Services & Stacks', 'docker', ARRAY['DCA', 'Orchestration', 'Swarm', 'Stacks', 'MKE', 'RBAC']::TEXT[], 39, 'advanced', true, 6, 60, 1, 0);

-- ── Section: Swarm Service Update Strategies & Rollback (7 questions) — Orchestration — Swarm service update strategies & rollback — authored from docs.docker.com's `docker service update`/`docker service create` CLI reference and the Swarm rolling-update tutorial; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material. ──

VALUES ('a99fedd9-d59e-4b89-9e08-667cfc38c4e5', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 1, 'The `--update-failure-action` flag on `docker service create`/`update` accepts which set of values?', 'Orchestration', 'update-failure-action Values', 'mcq');
VALUES ('a99fedd9-d59e-4b89-9e08-667cfc38c4e5', '4604f8f2-262c-4568-bf7d-3e8ef5b2145a', 'docs.docker.com confirms exactly three values: pause (the default — halts the rollout for manual intervention), continue (proceeds despite failures, risking a mixed-version cluster), and rollback (automatically reverts).', 'Orchestration — Swarm service update strategies & rollback — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker service update`/`docker service create` CLI reference and the Swarm rolling-update tutorial; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('ec504618-c109-406f-b4b6-62f868ca0ec1', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 2, 'With `--update-failure-action=rollback` configured, what specifically triggers the automatic rollback during a rolling update?', 'Orchestration', 'Automatic Rollback Trigger', 'mcq');
VALUES ('ec504618-c109-406f-b4b6-62f868ca0ec1', '98d01ea3-790a-480e-b1b5-80053ae54569', 'Automatic rollback under this setting is threshold-based: it fires once the observed failure ratio during the update exceeds --update-max-failure-ratio, not on the very first failure.', 'Orchestration — Swarm service update strategies & rollback — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker service update`/`docker service create` CLI reference and the Swarm rolling-update tutorial; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('623b5c79-7fcf-4599-a161-86e3b6eac5a0', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 3, 'What does setting `--update-order start-first` change about how Swarm performs a rolling update, compared to the default `stop-first`?', 'Orchestration', 'update-order: start-first vs. stop-first', 'mcq');
VALUES ('623b5c79-7fcf-4599-a161-86e3b6eac5a0', 'a51dc46a-2e70-4c2d-bb6e-4f0fe3694e04', 'start-first prioritizes availability by briefly overlapping old and new tasks (new one must be healthy before the old one stops), whereas the default stop-first tears down the old task before starting the replacement.', 'Orchestration — Swarm service update strategies & rollback — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker service update`/`docker service create` CLI reference and the Swarm rolling-update tutorial; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('254e5b40-9874-4cb6-88ea-41d7751319e6', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 4, 'A service is configured with `--update-parallelism 1 --rollback-parallelism 3`. What does this achieve?', 'Orchestration', 'Differing Update/Rollback Parallelism', 'mcq');
VALUES ('254e5b40-9874-4cb6-88ea-41d7751319e6', 'e33c1fd4-7b22-4906-8a69-d646f299acdd', 'Update and rollback parallelism are independently configurable — a common pattern is a cautious, slow rollout with a fast rollback path, since reverting to known-good code carries less risk than rolling forward.', 'Orchestration — Swarm service update strategies & rollback — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker service update`/`docker service create` CLI reference and the Swarm rolling-update tutorial; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('fa1c6cc0-17d7-4af3-aa60-45a86feecf54', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 5, 'Beyond an automatic rollback triggered by --update-failure-action=rollback, how can an operator manually revert a service to its previous spec after noticing a bad rollout?', 'Orchestration', 'Manual Rollback Command', 'mcq');
VALUES ('fa1c6cc0-17d7-4af3-aa60-45a86feecf54', '1b421b26-169d-42e5-a318-317162bb7000', 'Swarm retains the previous service spec specifically to support `docker service update --rollback`/`docker service rollback`, letting an operator revert without needing external state.', 'Orchestration — Swarm service update strategies & rollback — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker service update`/`docker service create` CLI reference and the Swarm rolling-update tutorial; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('f550c50d-18a6-4743-87ca-14d5ea32044c', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 6, 'What does the `--update-monitor` duration (e.g. `--update-monitor 30s`) control during a rolling update?', 'Orchestration', 'update-monitor Duration', 'mcq');
VALUES ('f550c50d-18a6-4743-87ca-14d5ea32044c', '07aef15f-d01b-45a5-b0e9-1f94e769f362', 'update-monitor is a per-task observation window — Swarm watches each updated task for this duration to catch failures (e.g. a crash loop) before considering that task''s update complete and proceeding.', 'Orchestration — Swarm service update strategies & rollback — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker service update`/`docker service create` CLI reference and the Swarm rolling-update tutorial; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('fc74fe38-0324-4690-a3f0-9fb2f56554b4', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 7, 'Distinct from update-monitor, what does `--update-delay` control?', 'Orchestration', 'update-delay Between Batches', 'mcq');
VALUES ('fc74fe38-0324-4690-a3f0-9fb2f56554b4', '761afbcf-cfac-4833-837c-a045aa566e53', 'update-delay is the inter-batch pacing control — after one parallelism-sized batch finishes (and its update-monitor window passes), Swarm waits this long before starting the next batch.', 'Orchestration — Swarm service update strategies & rollback — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker service update`/`docker service create` CLI reference and the Swarm rolling-update tutorial; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

-- ── Section: Placement Constraints & Preferences (7 questions) — Orchestration — Swarm placement constraints & preferences — authored from docs.docker.com's Swarm service placement documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material. ──

VALUES ('5bd0f1eb-10ae-478c-af9a-85c91856cfc8', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 8, 'Which of the following is a built-in Swarm placement constraint expression usable without any custom labeling, e.g. to restrict a service to manager nodes only?', 'Orchestration', 'Built-in Node Constraints', 'mcq');
VALUES ('5bd0f1eb-10ae-478c-af9a-85c91856cfc8', '7856dac3-ba7a-4325-b75f-f03afbcc802b', 'node.role is a built-in constraint key (values: manager or worker) that requires no custom label setup, unlike custom node.labels.* constraints.', 'Orchestration — Swarm placement constraints & preferences — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm service placement documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('2f49386f-6af4-4819-9d10-b4e656fe29f6', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 9, 'After running `docker node update --label-add zone=us-east node-3`, how would a service be constrained to place tasks only on nodes carrying that label?', 'Orchestration', 'Custom Node Label Constraints', 'mcq');
VALUES ('2f49386f-6af4-4819-9d10-b4e656fe29f6', '35972359-04df-4ca5-8be5-ad1721404668', 'Custom labels set via docker node update are referenced in constraints under the node.labels.<key> namespace, distinguishing them from Docker Engine daemon labels (engine.labels.*).', 'Orchestration — Swarm placement constraints & preferences — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm service placement documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('2b77f4f5-1d45-48b7-8746-d9f01ca33482', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 10, 'What is the distinction between a constraint referencing `engine.labels.<key>` versus one referencing `node.labels.<key>`?', 'Orchestration', 'engine.labels vs. node.labels', 'mcq');
VALUES ('2b77f4f5-1d45-48b7-8746-d9f01ca33482', '8d3719da-1c93-4256-9388-f237b6d62699', 'engine.labels come from the daemon''s own configuration (host-level, set independent of Swarm), while node.labels are Swarm-level metadata an administrator assigns via docker node update — both are valid constraint namespaces but sourced differently.', 'Orchestration — Swarm placement constraints & preferences — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm service placement documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('631c611a-859e-4e5b-a28b-ac1cfa69cdab', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 11, 'A service is created with both `--constraint ''node.labels.zone==us-east''` and `--constraint ''node.labels.tier==frontend''`. How are multiple --constraint flags combined?', 'Orchestration', 'Multiple Constraints — AND Logic', 'mcq');
VALUES ('631c611a-859e-4e5b-a28b-ac1cfa69cdab', '15afc80a-6361-40eb-9533-508c3cbbfd8e', 'Multiple constraints are ANDed together — every one must hold for a given node to be considered eligible, narrowing the eligible node set with each additional constraint.', 'Orchestration — Swarm placement constraints & preferences — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm service placement documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('667d47d4-47f3-4835-a5c4-8cd86c2e9040', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 12, 'What does the constraint `--constraint ''node.role!=worker''` express?', 'Orchestration', 'Constraint Inequality Operator', 'mcq');
VALUES ('667d47d4-47f3-4835-a5c4-8cd86c2e9040', 'e7fcfa62-7711-48d5-b64d-d182e831b755', 'Swarm constraint expressions support both == and != operators, so this is a valid (if slightly unusual, compared to just using node.role==manager) way to express the same restriction.', 'Orchestration — Swarm placement constraints & preferences — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm service placement documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('ac590ac9-d105-46c4-8f0f-12c49b9d47ec', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 13, 'How does a placement PREFERENCE (`--placement-pref ''spread=node.labels.zone''`) differ in effect from a placement CONSTRAINT?', 'Orchestration', 'Placement Preferences (Soft Spread)', 'mcq');
VALUES ('ac590ac9-d105-46c4-8f0f-12c49b9d47ec', 'f1d35fa5-15be-4091-93a9-27c3886d98d6', 'Placement preferences (spread) are a soft-scheduling hint for even distribution across a label''s values (e.g. balancing replicas across zones/racks); unlike constraints, they never make a node ineligible — they just influence which eligible node is chosen.', 'Orchestration — Swarm placement constraints & preferences — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm service placement documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('76a949f0-b2ef-4e3e-9494-9676dc027a1a', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 14, 'What does `--replicas-max-per-node` (used with `docker service create/update`) control?', 'Orchestration', 'max-replicas-per-node', 'mcq');
VALUES ('76a949f0-b2ef-4e3e-9494-9676dc027a1a', '53d874f7-1fef-4b92-8ea6-73450ce62cce', 'replicas-max-per-node caps per-node concentration of a single service''s tasks, which is a different concern from the service''s overall --replicas count (total desired tasks cluster-wide).', 'Orchestration — Swarm placement constraints & preferences — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm service placement documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

-- ── Section: Secrets & Configs as Swarm Service/Stack Resources (6 questions) — Orchestration — secrets/configs as Swarm service & stack resources — authored from docs.docker.com's Swarm configs/secrets documentation and Compose file reference (top-level configs:/secrets: keys); verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material. ──

VALUES ('98e31177-6c29-4992-b2b6-1f4b8dc6e42b', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 15, 'What does `docker config create app_config ./nginx.conf` do?', 'Orchestration', 'docker config create Basics', 'mcq');
VALUES ('98e31177-6c29-4992-b2b6-1f4b8dc6e42b', '698f26ef-6184-480d-8ad3-95d933dfc36d', 'docker config create registers a named config object from file content in the Swarm''s Raft store, available for later attachment to services — it doesn''t automatically attach or validate anything.', 'Orchestration — secrets/configs as Swarm service & stack resources — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm configs/secrets documentation and Compose file reference (top-level configs:/secrets: keys); verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('44281b51-fd23-4fc3-a48c-4e48e7f3be78', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 16, 'When creating a service with `--config source=app_config,target=/etc/nginx/nginx.conf`, what determines the file path the config is mounted at inside the task''s container?', 'Orchestration', 'Attaching a Config to a Service', 'mcq');
VALUES ('44281b51-fd23-4fc3-a48c-4e48e7f3be78', 'ceb5ce5c-77f2-4adf-82c0-7b3ab22578cd', 'The target parameter explicitly controls the in-container path, decoupling the config''s registered name from where it actually lands inside the container''s filesystem.', 'Orchestration — secrets/configs as Swarm service & stack resources — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm configs/secrets documentation and Compose file reference (top-level configs:/secrets: keys); verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('1d7f6319-a5f2-478d-8779-0fe2d9583d38', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 17, 'A Swarm service using a config is rescheduled from one worker node to another (e.g. after the original node fails). What happens to the config''s availability on the new node?', 'Orchestration', 'Configs Are Node-Portable', 'mcq');
VALUES ('1d7f6319-a5f2-478d-8779-0fe2d9583d38', '37dc2601-d28e-442e-885c-1d0d24fc45fd', 'Configs and secrets are both distributed via Swarm''s Raft-backed cluster state, not node-local files — rescheduling to any manager-approved node still delivers the config correctly.', 'Orchestration — secrets/configs as Swarm service & stack resources — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm configs/secrets documentation and Compose file reference (top-level configs:/secrets: keys); verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('8c9174ad-254c-4e08-b9bd-4ec961e1ac50', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 18, 'In a stack''s Compose file, a top-level secret is declared as `secrets: { db_password: { external: true } }`. What does `external: true` mean in this context?', 'Orchestration', 'Compose external: true for Configs/Secrets', 'mcq');
VALUES ('8c9174ad-254c-4e08-b9bd-4ec961e1ac50', '633a5743-f3ab-440c-9b49-bcd32a4d6525', 'external: true tells stack deploy the named secret/config is pre-existing and managed outside this Compose file''s lifecycle — deploy will fail if it doesn''t already exist, rather than attempting to create it.', 'Orchestration — secrets/configs as Swarm service & stack resources — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm configs/secrets documentation and Compose file reference (top-level configs:/secrets: keys); verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('dd8ef761-1a20-4363-a53f-74a8899d24f7', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 19, 'A Compose file for a stack declares a top-level secret `db_password` with `file: ./db_password.txt`, and a service references it under `secrets: [db_password]`. If the stack is deployed with `docker stack deploy -c compose.yml mystack`, what is the actual name of the created Swarm secret object?', 'Orchestration', 'Config/Secret Name Aliasing in Compose', 'mcq');
VALUES ('dd8ef761-1a20-4363-a53f-74a8899d24f7', 'c185710d-b1d7-404b-a4d2-b37b1517f7ed', 'Stack deploy namespaces top-level secrets/configs (and most other resources) under `<stackname>_<resourcename>`, so multiple stacks can each define a same-named `db_password` without colliding in the cluster''s global secret/config namespace.', 'Orchestration — secrets/configs as Swarm service & stack resources — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm configs/secrets documentation and Compose file reference (top-level configs:/secrets: keys); verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('af1de60d-a6cb-4306-9ff8-b897574ac26e', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 20, 'A running service currently uses `app_config`. To roll out a changed configuration file, what is the correct sequence, given config content (like secret content) is immutable once created?', 'Orchestration', 'Updating a Service''s Attached Configs', 'mcq');
VALUES ('af1de60d-a6cb-4306-9ff8-b897574ac26e', '2e6ca69d-9f0c-492b-a461-cb7a66e536ef', 'Like secrets, config content is immutable — updating it means creating a new config object and using --config-rm/--config-add on the service, which reschedules tasks to pick up the new attachment.', 'Orchestration — secrets/configs as Swarm service & stack resources — authored from docs.docker.com''s Swarm configs/secrets documentation and Compose file reference (top-level configs:/secrets: keys); verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

-- ── Section: Multi-Service Stack Deployment (7 questions) — Orchestration — multi-service stack deployment — authored from docs.docker.com's `docker stack deploy` CLI reference and Compose-file-for-stacks documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material. ──

VALUES ('cea6b5a1-b63f-404d-ac44-07a68d8bbbb7', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 21, 'What is the minimum Compose file format version required for a Compose file to be usable with `docker stack deploy`?', 'Orchestration', 'Minimum Compose Version for Stacks', 'mcq');
VALUES ('cea6b5a1-b63f-404d-ac44-07a68d8bbbb7', 'c83ef20e-c0a0-4500-98d6-3336e5ce53b0', 'The Compose v3 schema specifically introduced the deploy: key (replicas, placement, update_config, resources, etc.) needed to express Swarm-service concepts — v1/v2 files aren''t structured to carry that information.', 'Orchestration — multi-service stack deployment — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker stack deploy` CLI reference and Compose-file-for-stacks documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('9e5af0fc-28b7-48c7-bdc7-fdb4d821551e', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 22, 'A stack''s Compose file includes a service with a `build:` key instead of (or alongside) `image:`. What happens when this is deployed with `docker stack deploy`?', 'Orchestration', 'build: Key Ignored by Stack Deploy', 'mcq');
VALUES ('9e5af0fc-28b7-48c7-bdc7-fdb4d821551e', 'a1395dea-a612-4f2b-9278-a5931dad6159', 'Unlike `docker compose up` (which can build locally), `docker stack deploy` has no build step — images must already be built and available (usually via a shared registry) to every node that might run a task.', 'Orchestration — multi-service stack deployment — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker stack deploy` CLI reference and Compose-file-for-stacks documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('c0c6e699-0d43-4dd5-8e33-6a2f5e145a25', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 23, 'If a stack''s Compose file doesn''t declare a custom top-level `networks:` section, what networking do the stack''s services get by default?', 'Orchestration', 'Default Stack Networking', 'mcq');
VALUES ('c0c6e699-0d43-4dd5-8e33-6a2f5e145a25', 'a4631fc8-4561-4195-8dbb-64917ea00d4a', 'Stack deploy provisions a default stack-scoped overlay network when none is declared, so services can resolve and reach each other by name — this is analogous to Compose''s default network for `docker compose up`, but using the overlay driver instead of bridge.', 'Orchestration — multi-service stack deployment — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker stack deploy` CLI reference and Compose-file-for-stacks documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('0015b1d3-33c3-4bbe-833f-71ab581ce942', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 24, 'What does `docker stack ps mystack` show, as distinct from `docker stack services mystack`?', 'Orchestration', 'docker stack ps', 'mcq');
VALUES ('0015b1d3-33c3-4bbe-833f-71ab581ce942', 'aaad6b8d-a95e-4e26-a8a7-b1e955b05b0a', 'stack ps operates at task granularity (like docker service ps, but across the whole stack), while stack services summarizes at the service level (replica counts, image, ports) — different levels of detail for different debugging needs.', 'Orchestration — multi-service stack deployment — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker stack deploy` CLI reference and Compose-file-for-stacks documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('5f5a00b5-9506-4d28-9ece-0776591df8db', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 25, 'After editing a stack''s Compose file (e.g. bumping an image tag), what is the correct way to apply the change to the running stack?', 'Orchestration', 'Redeploying an Updated Stack', 'mcq');
VALUES ('5f5a00b5-9506-4d28-9ece-0776591df8db', '624f1021-d02f-4175-9994-660e3565df07', 'docker stack deploy is idempotent/declarative — re-running it against the same stack name reconciles differences (new image, changed replica count, etc.) without requiring a teardown first.', 'Orchestration — multi-service stack deployment — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker stack deploy` CLI reference and Compose-file-for-stacks documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('065a6033-a19e-413b-8e13-ab2a51e19db8', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 26, 'A stack named `mystack` defines a service called `web` in its Compose file. What is the actual Swarm service name created?', 'Orchestration', 'Stack Resource Naming/Prefixing', 'mcq');
VALUES ('065a6033-a19e-413b-8e13-ab2a51e19db8', '5b9541b3-f31e-482f-bbdd-554311896d24', 'Consistent with how stack deploy namespaces secrets/configs/networks, services are also prefixed as <stackname>_<servicename>, letting the same short service name be reused safely across different stacks.', 'Orchestration — multi-service stack deployment — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker stack deploy` CLI reference and Compose-file-for-stacks documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('eea8655b-6c71-4ea5-b222-b5ab34add9ed', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 27, 'What does `docker stack rm mystack` remove?', 'Orchestration', 'docker stack rm Scope', 'mcq');
VALUES ('eea8655b-6c71-4ea5-b222-b5ab34add9ed', '7fd23533-db52-4739-956b-73491dec8b9e', 'stack rm tears down the resources that stack deploy itself created and owns for that stack; resources marked external: true were never owned by the stack, so they''re left alone.', 'Orchestration — multi-service stack deployment — authored from docs.docker.com''s `docker stack deploy` CLI reference and Compose-file-for-stacks documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

-- ── Section: Swarm Overlay Networking Specifics (6 questions) — Orchestration — Swarm overlay networking specifics — authored from docs.docker.com's overlay network driver and 'Manage swarm service networks' documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material. ──

VALUES ('d809071c-08b2-4f75-9dda-acbc8239f5db', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 28, 'How is application-data encryption enabled for traffic on a specific overlay network between Swarm nodes?', 'Orchestration', 'Creating an Encrypted Overlay Network', 'mcq');
VALUES ('d809071c-08b2-4f75-9dda-acbc8239f5db', '13731ca0-7feb-4516-9fa9-7353447f3f60', 'The --opt encrypted flag on network create (overlay driver) turns on IPSEC-based encryption of the VXLAN data plane for that specific network — application data among Swarm nodes is NOT encrypted by default.', 'Orchestration — Swarm overlay networking specifics — authored from docs.docker.com''s overlay network driver and ''Manage swarm service networks'' documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('aeba9dbc-c3b3-48e2-9eaa-970eb5b503e5', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 29, 'What is the documented trade-off of enabling `--opt encrypted` on an overlay network?', 'Orchestration', 'Encrypted Overlay Trade-off', 'mcq');
VALUES ('aeba9dbc-c3b3-48e2-9eaa-970eb5b503e5', 'c64c25d9-8795-455b-a6e1-e42b5f4534e5', 'docs.docker.com explicitly documents the performance cost of overlay encryption and calls out that it isn''t supported for Windows containers on an encrypted overlay network.', 'Orchestration — Swarm overlay networking specifics — authored from docs.docker.com''s overlay network driver and ''Manage swarm service networks'' documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('c1dcd024-52ed-4238-8182-07cdeadd0daf', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 30, 'What automatically creates the special `ingress` overlay network, and what is its role?', 'Orchestration', 'The ingress Network', 'mcq');
VALUES ('c1dcd024-52ed-4238-8182-07cdeadd0daf', 'b86d5a5b-5f9e-4e90-92dc-a7dab934625a', 'ingress is provisioned automatically as part of swarm initialization/joining, and by default backs the routing mesh for services published without a custom overlay network.', 'Orchestration — Swarm overlay networking specifics — authored from docs.docker.com''s overlay network driver and ''Manage swarm service networks'' documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('995f7217-6d07-441c-b06b-0bcc3749b8e4', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 31, 'What does the `--attachable` flag on `docker network create --driver overlay` enable that isn''t possible on a non-attachable overlay network?', 'Orchestration', 'Overlay Network Scope: attachable', 'mcq');
VALUES ('995f7217-6d07-441c-b06b-0bcc3749b8e4', 'd5dab760-632f-412f-8120-e792788b15ce', 'By default, Swarm overlay networks are only usable by Swarm service tasks; --attachable specifically opens the network up so standalone containers can also join it via docker run --network.', 'Orchestration — Swarm overlay networking specifics — authored from docs.docker.com''s overlay network driver and ''Manage swarm service networks'' documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('db644d4d-f033-4d60-877b-d9ca756f99d8', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 32, 'For the overlay driver''s VXLAN data plane to function correctly between nodes, which port/protocol must be open in addition to the Swarm management ports (2377/tcp, 7946/tcp+udp)?', 'Orchestration', 'Overlay Network Underlying Ports', 'mcq');
VALUES ('db644d4d-f033-4d60-877b-d9ca756f99d8', 'cbfc2885-5066-4ec6-aa70-edbb5483121f', 'VXLAN, the encapsulation protocol overlay networking uses, communicates over UDP/4789 — this must be open between nodes alongside the Swarm control-plane ports (2377/tcp for manager join, 7946/tcp+udp for the gossip/discovery protocol).', 'Orchestration — Swarm overlay networking specifics — authored from docs.docker.com''s overlay network driver and ''Manage swarm service networks'' documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

VALUES ('eb9d275c-a063-42d0-9bc8-70c544863424', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 33, 'What is the fundamental scope difference between Docker''s `overlay` network driver and its `bridge` network driver?', 'Orchestration', 'Overlay vs. Bridge Driver Scope', 'mcq');
VALUES ('eb9d275c-a063-42d0-9bc8-70c544863424', 'f0b559c7-8c81-4000-9ae3-440e41a6bcfc', 'This is the core distinction motivating overlay''s existence: bridge networking works only within one Docker host, while overlay uses VXLAN encapsulation to let containers on different hosts communicate as though co-located.', 'Orchestration — Swarm overlay networking specifics — authored from docs.docker.com''s overlay network driver and ''Manage swarm service networks'' documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker exam material.');

-- ── Section: Mirantis Kubernetes Engine (MKE) — RBAC, Teams & Organizations (6 questions) — Orchestration — Mirantis Kubernetes Engine (MKE) RBAC, teams & organizations — authored from docs.mirantis.com's MKE role-based access control and grants documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker/Mirantis exam material. ──

VALUES ('7b83713b-7b6d-4ce6-9140-485d15de802e', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 34, 'In MKE''s access-control model, what is a ''grant'', structurally?', 'Orchestration', 'The Grant Model', 'mcq');
VALUES ('7b83713b-7b6d-4ce6-9140-485d15de802e', '0db30d91-6e27-48d4-a6f3-bbfed245434b', 'MKE''s own documentation describes a grant as exactly this triple: a specific subject, given a specific role, over a specific resource set — the basic unit of MKE''s RBAC system.', 'Orchestration — Mirantis Kubernetes Engine (MKE) RBAC, teams & organizations — authored from docs.mirantis.com''s MKE role-based access control and grants documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker/Mirantis exam material.');

VALUES ('9c6c0707-b010-41ff-ab2c-1d37ac8498c1', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 35, 'How does MKE group cluster resources for the purpose of RBAC grants, and does this differ between its Swarm and Kubernetes orchestration modes?', 'Orchestration', 'Resource Sets: Collections vs. Namespaces', 'mcq');
VALUES ('9c6c0707-b010-41ff-ab2c-1d37ac8498c1', 'b4ae70ad-8345-4a46-b9e1-82286c78093c', 'MKE documentation explicitly distinguishes Swarm ''collections'' from Kubernetes namespaces as the two orchestrator-specific ways cluster resources are grouped for grant targeting.', 'Orchestration — Mirantis Kubernetes Engine (MKE) RBAC, teams & organizations — authored from docs.mirantis.com''s MKE role-based access control and grants documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker/Mirantis exam material.');

VALUES ('35b31c62-d8e2-4b48-9b4e-ae013fd76aac', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 36, 'In MKE, what is the relationship between an ''organization'' and a ''team'' when selecting a grant''s subject?', 'Orchestration', 'Organizations and Teams', 'mcq');
VALUES ('35b31c62-d8e2-4b48-9b4e-ae013fd76aac', '287d52bb-f06f-4432-a053-74e8fec642b4', 'MKE''s grant-creation workflow lets an admin pick an Organization and then optionally a Team within it, letting access be scoped more finely than ''the whole organization'' when needed.', 'Orchestration — Mirantis Kubernetes Engine (MKE) RBAC, teams & organizations — authored from docs.mirantis.com''s MKE role-based access control and grants documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker/Mirantis exam material.');

VALUES ('caa356a3-d9ec-44b9-b64e-49e2890e483a', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 37, 'Besides individual users, organizations, and teams, what other subject type can an MKE grant be issued to?', 'Orchestration', 'Service Accounts as Grant Subjects', 'mcq');
VALUES ('caa356a3-d9ec-44b9-b64e-49e2890e483a', '9a944b98-726c-47b5-80b3-e3e1964210fd', 'MKE''s grant subject options include Users, Organizations (with optional Team), and Service Accounts — covering both human and automated/non-human access patterns under the same grant model.', 'Orchestration — Mirantis Kubernetes Engine (MKE) RBAC, teams & organizations — authored from docs.mirantis.com''s MKE role-based access control and grants documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker/Mirantis exam material.');

VALUES ('87163114-7b03-4817-85e7-25c79bfe834c', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 38, 'What is the difference between an MKE ''default role'' and a ''custom role'' in the context of building a grant?', 'Orchestration', 'Default vs. Custom Roles', 'mcq');
VALUES ('87163114-7b03-4817-85e7-25c79bfe834c', '0f1f4b81-a214-44aa-80c4-bde200ccedaf', 'MKE ships default roles as common starting points, but also supports custom roles built by explicitly selecting which API operations are permitted per resource type — for access patterns the defaults don''t cover.', 'Orchestration — Mirantis Kubernetes Engine (MKE) RBAC, teams & organizations — authored from docs.mirantis.com''s MKE role-based access control and grants documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker/Mirantis exam material.');

VALUES ('9cf34129-f6e3-4e04-8cd7-7cf8f23ae829', '159e0a4f-6de1-407e-a236-0e49856968a8', 39, 'When creating a Kubernetes-oriented grant in MKE, what does enabling the ''Cluster Role Binding'' switch do, as opposed to leaving it off?', 'Orchestration', 'Cluster Role Binding Switch for Kubernetes', 'mcq');
VALUES ('9cf34129-f6e3-4e04-8cd7-7cf8f23ae829', 'e8a74d18-3ac4-4d9f-b0c2-f89121f1a521', 'The Cluster Role Binding switch is how an MKE administrator chooses between a namespace-scoped grant and a cluster-wide one when working with Kubernetes-orchestrated resources.', 'Orchestration — Mirantis Kubernetes Engine (MKE) RBAC, teams & organizations — authored from docs.mirantis.com''s MKE role-based access control and grants documentation; verified via web search 2026-09-04; not copied from official Docker/Mirantis exam material.');
